For each word below, write ONE short sentence (12 to 22 words) that uses the word itself, spelled in full, in the sense given. Give it voice and mood: a question, someone speaking, a sigh, delight, a warning. No definitions; show the word in a moment of life. Answer as one JSON object mapping each WORD (as given, upper case) to its sentence. JSON only.

ORGANIC: a fertilizer that is derived from animal or vegetable matter.
ORPHAN: a child who has lost both parents.
OVERLAP: a representation of common ground between theories or phenomena.
OWNER: (law) someone who owns (is legal possessor of) a business.
PACKAGE: a collection of things wrapped or boxed together.
PANEL: sheet that forms a distinct (usually flat and rectangular) section or component of something.
PASS: (baseball) an advance to first base by a batter who receives four balls.
PHASE: any distinct time period in a sequence of events.
PHOTON: a quantum of electromagnetic radiation.
PIN: a piece of jewelry that is pinned onto the wearer's garment.
PIVOT: the person in a rank around whom the others wheel and maneuver.
PLASMA: the colorless watery fluid of the blood and lymph that contains no cells, but in which the blood cells (erythrocytes, leukocytes, and thrombocytes) are suspended.
